title: MarciaStart
---
<<declare $npcName = "Marcia">> //The NPC's name will go here and can be different for each NPC if needed
<<declare $charName = "Marc">>

//I currently don't have assigned welcomes for each dialogue like I do for the rest of it, so many welcomes may not look like they fit, may be repeated, or no welcome at all

{$npcName}: This tree gives off a lot of mixed feelings. A lot of things that many would like to forget, but others would like to remember.
-> <i>Listen to their story</i>
    <<jump MarciaStory>>
-> <i>Ask about their day</i>
    <<jump MarciaDay>>
-> <i>Back to the lobby</i>
===

title: MarciaStory
---
Do you want to listen to the story?
-> <i>Yes</i>
    <<jump MarciaStoryStart>>
-> <i>No</i>
===

title: MarciaStoryStart
---
<<wait 4>>
===

title: MarciaDay
---
{$npcName}: Today is a great day. The sky is clear, the flowers smell amazing, and birds are singing their little hearts out. I just wish every day was like this.
-> I like that mindset!
    <<jump DayGood>>
-> A little rain here and there never hurts.
    <<jump DayNeutral>>
-> Nothing too special.
    <<jump DayBad>>
===

title: DayGood
---
{$npcName}: You should always be positive, even if things are dark for a moment.
===

title: DayNeutral
---
{$npcName}: You're not wrong there. Rain is always good for nature.
===

title: DayBad
---
{$npcName}: Oh...well...you should still be greatful for days like this.
===